  "date": "2026-08-16",
  "purpose": "Test whether Phase 11B's single-model/single-context/5-prompt sensitivity ranking generalizes: across a full 31-prompt set and 11 task categories (prompt/category stability), across SmolLM2-135M vs 360M (model stability), across ctx=2048 vs ctx=8192 (context stability), and whether a ranking built only from held-out training prompts beats naive layouts on prompts it never saw (policy usefulness).",
  "literal_verdict": null,
  "literal_verdict_note": "This phase's own summary.json does not record a single decision_gate/classification-style literal constant like its sibling phases -- its result is a structured multi-question answer set (research_questions_answered) plus a decision_gate_inputs object. Reporting the literal fields directly rather than inventing a constant that doesn't exist in source.",
  "verdict_summary": "Mixed, precisely disclosed: (1) full-ranking prompt-to-prompt stability is only modest (Spearman rho 0.36-0.47), but a small set of 2-3 layers per model are overwhelmingly and consistently the most sensitive across nearly every prompt; (2) category-level stability is strong (rho 0.55-0.93, same top layers dominate every category); (3) cross-model stability is modest at exact layer-index level but moderate at normalized-depth level (both models' most-sensitive layer sits at ~93-97% depth); (4) cross-context (2048 vs 8192) stability is fairly strong (rho 0.71, top-2 layers identical and same order) with a disclosed caveat that both settings consumed similar actual token counts; (5) a ranking built from only 21 training prompts clearly beat every naive layout on logit_rel_l2 at every held-out Q8-budget tested, and won or tied on top1_preservation at 5/6 budgets -- delta_nll was mixed, with random sometimes winning at low budgets. Net: the top few sensitive layers are stable and the resulting policy usefully beats naive baselines out-of-sample, but the full ranking's stability is genuinely partial, not strong across the board -- disclosed as such, not glossed over.",
  "verdict_source": "results/canonical/summary.json: research_questions_answered (all 5 sub-answers), decision_gate_inputs; results/canonical/holdout_policy.json: headline_finding (literal source fields, not synthesized)",
  "productized": false,
